# Expectation record for 14_abi_calling_convention/006_nested_calls_callee_saved.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 006_nested_calls_callee_saved
area               = 14_abi_calling_convention
description        = A nine-frame chain of genuinely out-of-line calls -- eight pressure frames above one leaf -- in which each pressure frame keeps ten independent values live across its nested call and prints them only after that call returns, so that a callee-saved register the callee failed to restore shows up in the output of each frame it affects -- and where a wrong value propagates down the chain, in the first frame whose line differs and in every later frame that reads it
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Free of undefined and unspecified behaviour by construction:
- THE SHAPE OF THE CHAIN, stated exactly, because every claim below rests on it. Nine
  frames: level1 through level8, then leaf_mix. The EIGHT levels are the pressure frames --
  each reads its own row of the volatile tables, makes its nested call, and prints all ten
  values afterwards. leaf_mix is the ninth frame and is NOT a pressure frame: it makes no
  call, so it holds nothing across one, and it owns no table row. The tables are therefore
  eight rows deep, matching what is consumed rather than the frame count.
- No signed integer overflow, and the arithmetic is small and enumerable. The seed enters at
  100 and grows by 10 per level, reaching 180 at leaf_mix, whose result is
  180 + (int)(9.0 * 4.0) = 216. Each pressure frame returns its callee's result plus the six
  integers of its own row, and every row sums to -3 (for example 3101 - 3102 + 3103 - 3104 +
  3105 - 3106), so the chain returns 216 - 8 * 3 = 192 and every intermediate value lies
  between 192 and 216. The largest magnitude anywhere in the program is the table entry
  3806 -- more than five orders of magnitude short of INT_MAX, which is 2147483647 even on
  i686's 32-bit int.
- The printed values are NOT derived from the seed. Each pressure frame's ten values are read
  from static volatile tables: six ints from vlive_i (3101 through 3806, alternating sign),
  three doubles from vlive_d (1.25 through 24.75), and one pointer from vlive_p designating
  an entry of plive_target (5101 through 5808). All forty-eight integers, all twenty-four
  doubles and all eight pointed-to integers are distinct, which is what makes a value
  restored from the wrong slot name both the frame and the position it came from. Deriving
  them from the seed instead would let the optimizer rematerialize them after the call and
  hold nothing across it, which would leave the program asserting ten values while requiring
  none to survive.
- Every floating value is a dyadic rational -- a whole number of quarters -- so it is exactly
  representable in binary64, and every printed value carries an explicit precision with room
  to spare, so no rounding decision is taken and i686's x87 extended intermediate precision
  cannot perturb a result. No non-finite value, no negative zero and no division appears. The
  one floating-to-integer conversion multiplies by 4.0 first, so its integral part is exact
  and small.
- No shift operator appears, so no shift count can be out of range.
- THE ONLY INDEXING IS INTO THE PROGRAM'S OWN STATIC TABLES, with constant subscripts written
  literally at each use -- vlive_i[6][3] and the like -- so the pointer arithmetic the language
  performs for each subscript stays inside the object by inspection and no computed index
  exists. The only pointer values are the address of a string literal threaded through the chain
  as a tag, and the eight addresses of plive_target elements formed once by &plive_target[k]
  with literal k and held in vlive_p; a pointer is dereferenced only to print the int it
  designates, and none is printed, converted to an integer, compared against a pointer into a
  different object, or modified. No pointer arithmetic beyond those in-bounds subscripts is
  performed anywhere, and no one-past-the-end pointer is formed.
- No read of uninitialized storage. Every local of all nine chain functions is initialized at
  its declaration, and every volatile object has a static initializer. main's five locals are
  the one deliberate exception to the declaration form: they are declared and then assigned,
  each before its first read, because the runtime entry has to stage its three volatile
  operands one read per full statement, which an initializer list of declarations could not
  express. Assignment-before-read is the property that matters, and it holds for all five.
- No object is modified twice between sequence points.
- Recursion is absent: every level calls a DIFFERENT function and the depth is a fixed nine
  frames plus main, so termination is structural. There is no iteration statement anywhere
  in the program either -- no for, no while, no do -- and no goto and no switch, so control
  flow is straight-line through a fixed chain of calls and cannot fail to terminate. The
  runtime entry point likewise stages its three volatile operands with three straight-line
  statements rather than a loop.
- NOTHING DEPENDS ON UNSPECIFIED EVALUATION ORDER, and this is enforced structurally
  rather than argued. An access to a volatile object IS an observable side effect and the
  order in which a call's arguments are evaluated is unspecified, so every volatile datum
  is read exactly once, in a statement of its own, and only the resulting plain locals are
  passed. Machine-checked: flattening the program into statements and
  counting references to its volatile objects finds NO statement with more than one. The
  snapshots cost nothing in coverage, because each is itself a load from volatile storage
  that the optimizer may neither fold nor elide, so every value the callee receives was
  genuinely materialised at run time and marshalled through the ABI; what changed is only
  that the loads are now SEQUENCED rather than unordered.
- Hermetic, as constraint C4 requires: every input is a literal in the source. Nothing is
  opened, no socket is created, no environment variable and no program argument is read,
  and no storage is obtained from the heap.
- main returns 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires.
- Verified rather than asserted: the default strict warning gate
  (-Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror) produces zero
  diagnostics in the single native compile-only invocation the suite makes of it, and
  -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all runs to completion with empty
  stderr and exit status 0 in its one instrumented native build.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
THE PRESERVED REGISTER SETS, STATED IN FULL. What follows is what each ABI REQUIRES a
callee to preserve. It is not a claim about how any compiler chooses to allocate, which is
the compiler's business and not something a test may assume.
  System V AMD64  rbx, rbp, r12, r13, r14, r15 (and rsp). There is NO callee-saved SSE or
                  x87 DATA register at all; the x87 control word and the mxcsr control bits
                  are preserved, but no data register is.
  System V i386   ebx, esi, edi and EBP (and esp) -- four, the narrowest set of the four,
                  and likewise no callee-saved floating-point data register.
  AAPCS64         x19-x28, plus x29 as the frame pointer (x30 is the link register, saved by
                  the caller's own prologue). For the SIMD/FP file the obligation is PARTIAL
                  and precise: only the LOW 64 BITS of v8-v15, that is d8-d15, are
                  preserved; the upper bits of those registers, like the whole of v0-v7 and
                  v16-v31, are not.
  LP64D           s0-s11 integer, where s0 doubles as the frame pointer, and fs0-fs11
                  floating.

WHAT THE PROGRAM ASSERTS, AND WHAT IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT. Each of the EIGHT pressure
frames keeps six ints, three doubles and one pointer live ACROSS its nested call and prints
them only after that call returns; the ninth frame, the leaf, makes no call and so holds
nothing across one. Ten live values is more than the narrowest of those preserved sets can
hold, so on every target some of them must survive the call somewhere other than a preserved
register -- but which value goes where is the compiler's choice, and this program does not
assert it. What it asserts is the OBSERVABLE consequence: if any of the ten fails to survive
the call, the printed line for that frame changes, so the divergence is localised to the frames it
actually reaches rather than summarised -- one frame where a single register is clobbered, and every
affected frame where the failure is systemic. Eighty values are held across a call in total, ten in
each of eight frames, and every one of the eighty reaches its frame's own printed line, so every one
is detected there. The chain's returned total of 192 is printed as well, and it is a SECOND, partial
witness rather than a duplicate of the first: each frame returns inner + a + b + c + d + e + f, so
only the SIX INTS of a frame feed the total. A lost int therefore shows up twice, once in its
frame's line and once in the total; a lost double or a lost pointer shows up once, in its frame's
line alone, because neither x, y, z nor *p is summed into the return value. Both are caught; only the
redundancy differs. The total therefore covers six of a frame's ten live values, not all ten, and
saying otherwise would overstate what the second witness establishes.

THE TWO LIVE POINTERS, AND WHY THEIR WIDTH IS THE ONE THING ABOUT THEM THAT DIFFERS. Each
pressure frame holds two pointers across its nested call: the const char *tag it was handed,
which it needs again for the %s of the line it prints afterwards, and the const int *p it read
from vlive_p, which is one of its ten independent values. These are the only live values whose
storage size is not the same on all four targets -- sizeof(void *) was measured as 4 on i686
and 8 on x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64 -- so whichever preserved register or spill slot each
pointer occupies is half as wide on i686 as elsewhere, which is exactly why a pointer is worth
carrying live here rather than only integers and doubles. Neither pointer's VALUE reaches the
output. The tag is printed with %s, which emits the string it designates; p is dereferenced and
printed with %d, which emits the int it designates. So the printed text cannot depend on where
anything was placed, while the callee-saved obligation is still exercised at whatever pointer
width the target defines.

THE CALL BARRIER, AND WHAT IT IS AND IS NOT. Every call this program makes to the function
whose ABI boundary is under test goes through a FILE-SCOPE volatile FUNCTION POINTER, and
that is load-bearing rather than stylistic. WHAT ISO C REQUIRES: an access to a volatile
object is a side effect belonging to the observable behaviour an implementation must
reproduce (C11 5.1.2.3p2 and p6), and C11 6.7.3p7 requires an expression referring to a
volatile-qualified object to be evaluated strictly according to the abstract machine's rules
-- so the pointer must be RE-READ at each point of call, no conforming compiler may establish
at translation time which function it designates, and control must be transferred to whatever
function that particular load produced. WHAT ISO C DOES NOT REQUIRE: that the transfer reaches
the callee's original entry point, nor that a frame survives as a frame. A conforming
implementation may introduce a specialised clone or perform guarded devirtualization that
elides a frame on the matching path, and still honour the loaded value, because the observable
behaviour is unchanged. So the barrier must NOT be described as making the callee "neither
inlinable nor cloneable": that claims more than anything the standard says. It is an optimization
OBSTACLE whose effect is measured on named artifacts, never a language guarantee, and the residual
risk that leaves is real: a compiler under test
that devirtualized through a specialised entry could collapse a frame while still printing the
same bytes, and this program would not detect it. Closing that would take a per-cell STATIC
check of the artifact the compiler under test emitted -- nine frames present, ten indirect
transfers, no .constprop, .isra or .part. clone -- which is a harness capability this suite does
not have and which no oracle here substitutes for, so the chain depth claimed for a compiler
under test extends exactly as far as that artifact inspection.
001_many_integer_parameters.expected carries the same statement for this whole area. This is
plain standard C rather than a compiler attribute, so both sides of oracle (a) honour it for
the same reason and neither needs to support an extension for the barrier to hold. It also
makes the function-pointer load the ONLY volatile access in each call expression, which is what
keeps the one-side-effecting-argument rule satisfied.

MEASURED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS, on the reference drivers' own artifacts. WITHOUT the
barrier, called by name, the reference compiler at -O2 leaves only level1 standing -- levels 2
through 8 and the leaf are all inlined into it, so the nine frames would collapse to one and
the property under test would not exist at that optimization level. WITH it, all nine
functions are emitted unmodified at -O0, -O1 and -O2 on all four targets, with no .constprop
and no .isra clone anywhere.

MEASURED STACK USE, not estimated. From the reference compiler's -O0 prologues on each
target: x86_64 eight 96-byte frames plus one 48 and one 32, with ten 8-byte return-address
and frame-pointer saves, about 1.0 KiB; i686 eight 84-byte frames plus one 36 and one 32,
with ten 4-byte saves, about 0.8 KiB; aarch64 eight 128-byte frames plus one 64 and one 48,
about 1.1 KiB; riscv64 eight 160-byte frames plus one 64 and one 48, about 1.4 KiB -- the
deepest of the four, and the one whose figure is easiest to guess wrong from the scalar count.
On aarch64 and riscv64 the return-address and frame-pointer saves sit inside the figure
quoted, because the prologue stores them within the frame it has just allocated; on x86_64 and
i686 they sit outside it, which is why those two carry the saves as a separate term. The C
library's own printf frame sits on top of all four and is not counted. So the honest figure is
one to two kibibytes rather than a few hundred bytes, which the ten-scalar count alone would
have suggested and which the measurement contradicts. It stays roughly three orders of
magnitude below the 8 MiB default stack these binaries run under, both natively (ulimit -s
reports 8192 KiB) and under QEMU user-mode emulation (QEMU_STACK_SIZE defaults to 8388608
bytes).

Plain char signedness is implementation-defined and was measured as signed on x86_64 and
i686 and unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64; no plain-char value is printed. sizeof(long) and
sizeof(void *) were measured as 4 on i686 and 8 on x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64
(docs/technical-specifications.md lines 457-462); no long, size_t, ptrdiff_t, intptr_t or
pointer value is printed and no long or pointer conversion specification is used. long
double has three different representations across the four targets (measured 16, 12, 16 and
16 bytes; x87 80-bit versus IEEE binary128) and is absent from this program entirely --
using it would import a difference that has nothing to do with parameter passing. That
type is covered by 13_floating_point/004_long_double_target_restricted, whose record
disables oracle (b) alone, with the measured reason recorded and the expected-divergence
marker XD-TYPE-LONGDOUBLE-001 scoping that oracle.

No target is dropped, no oracle is disabled and this record carries no expected-divergence
marker: a cross-backend divergence here is a GENUINE FINDING rather than an
implementation-defined difference, because nothing implementation-defined reaches the
output. Measured rather than assumed: stdout is byte-identical and the exit status is 0 in all
twelve target-and-optimization-level cells.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
